WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.730
In 2025, the Keep It On coalition
recorded at least 313 internet shutdowns,

2
00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:09.470
in 52 countries.

3
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.490
Myanmar alone had at least 95.

4
00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:15.890
For the third year, conflict
was the lead trigger.

5
00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:20.190
On 4 June 2021, Nigeria suspended Twitter.

6
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:25.430
In April 2017, Turkey blocked every
language version of Wikipedia.

7
00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:28.330
Can citizens win back
the freedom to connect?

8
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.750
Or do governments always win?

9
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.070
In this mission, you'll
meet civil society,

10
00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:39.110
and a global coalition of over 370
organisations that documents shutdowns.

11
00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:44.030
Then you'll follow both cases, from
the first block to what happened next.

12
00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:48.850
Your mission: evaluate whether citizens
can win back the freedom to connect.
